          "text": "I expect the ball to rise toward the hoop but fall short of the opening. The air density and spinning-ball fluid model are active: the strong backspin produces Magnus lift, including a substantial force opposing forward motion during the ascent. Those forces make this trajectory quite different from a gravity-only throw. I have not run the simulation, so this is a physics-based prediction rather than an observed result.\n\nThe correction below disables aerodynamic forces and uses a ballistic launch. The ball\u2019s center reaches approximately `(4, 0, 3.05)` after 1.6 seconds, descending steeply enough to clear the rim.\n\n```xml\n<mujoco model=\"basketball_hoop\">\n  <option timestep=\"0.002\" gravity=\"0 0 -9.81\" density=\"0\" viscosity=\"0\"/>\n\n  <visual>\n    <headlight ambient=\"0.15 0.15 0.15\" diffuse=\"0.3 0.3 0.3\" specular=\"0 0 0\"/>\n  </visual>\n\n  <worldbody>\n    <light name=\"overhead_sun\" directional=\"true\" pos=\"2 0 10\" dir=\"0 0 -1\" diffuse=\"0.8 0.8 0.8\" specular=\"0.2 0.2 0.2\" castshadow=\"true\"/>\n    <light name=\"overhead_fill\" pos=\"4 0 8\" dir=\"0 0 -1\" diffuse=\"0.3 0.3 0.3\" specular=\"0 0 0\" castshadow=\"false\"/>\n\n    <geom name=\"floor\" type=\"plane\" pos=\"0 0 0\" size=\"10 10 0.1\" rgba=\"0.72 0.52 0.32 1\" friction=\"0.8 0.005 0.0001\"/>\n\n    <!-- Regulation size-7 basketball, initially touching the floor. -->\n    <body name=\"ball\" pos=\"0 0 0.1194\">\n      <freejoint name=\"ball_free\"/>\n      <inertial pos=\"0 0 0\" mass=\"0.62\" diaginertia=\"0.005893 0.005893 0.005893\"/>\n      <geom name=\"ball\" type=\"sphere\" size=\"0.1194\" rgba=\"0.85 0.40 0.10 1\" friction=\"0.9 0.01 0.001\" solref=\"0.01 0.2\"/>\n    </body>\n\n    <!-- Fixed hoop, with its origin at the rim center. -->\n    <body name=\"hoop\" pos=\"4 0 3.05\">\n      <geom name=\"rim_00\" type=\"capsule\" size=\"0.008\" fromto=\"0.2366 0 0 0.2186 0.0905 0\" rgba=\"0.9 0.3 0.05 1\"/>\n      <geom name=\"rim_01\" type=\"capsul